The source code, design, and documentation of SruthiScribe (the transcription
engine, the web application, the evaluation harness under tools/, and the
accompanying materials) are the copyrighted work of Vinoth Kannan. The source
being publicly visible does not grant a licence: no part of it may be copied,
modified, redistributed, or used to build derivative works without prior
written permission from the copyright holder.

Using the hosted application to transcribe your own singing is what it is
for; the notation you produce from your own recordings is yours.

This copyright does NOT extend to third-party material the application
carries or draws on, each of which keeps its own terms:

- Notation from Subbarama Dikshitar's Sangita Sampradaya Pradarsini (1904)
  is in the public domain. The typesetting of the English web edition
  belongs to the Guruguhanugraha Archives.
- Compositions, notation, and audio in the community library carry the
  source and licence recorded on each entry (public-domain, CC BY, or
  contributor-shared), shown alongside the entry in the application.
- The Sanidha dataset (Georgia Tech) is CC BY 4.0; one attributed excerpt
  from it is served in the library with performer, source, and licence shown
  beside the player. The Saraga dataset (CompMusic/UPF) is used for accuracy
  measurement only; none of its audio or annotations are redistributed.

